{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id33517632"}, "name":{"label":"mc_CLOUD"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2021-11-30T12:55:14-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"21.13"}, "id":{"label":"8080991646"}, "title":{"label":"Multiple uses and functionality…at a premium"}, "content":{"label":"Like you, I’ve tested and/or purchased every major productivity app. Due is a near-perfect blend of simplicity and functionality. What gets annoying are the incremental charges for standard “features” (cross-device use, full unlock, etc.). I refuse to pay Due a fourth time for widget access (one of my favorite and most-used iOS capabilities). \nAs a developer, I understand the costs other indie developers occur, however, this isn’t 2011 and last year, after taking their excessive 30% cut, Apple distributed $300B USD to developers (half of that went to game devs).", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=390017969&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
